   "sketch": "1. Let x = |a+b| and y = |a|+|b|. Then x ≥ 0 and y ≥ 0.\n2. By the triangle inequality, x = |a+b| ≤ |a|+|b| = y.\n3. The function f(t)=t/(1+t) is increasing on [0,∞): if 0 ≤ x ≤ y, then x/(1+x) ≤ y/(1+y), since cross-multiplying gives x(1+y) ≤ y(1+x), equivalent to x ≤ y.\n4. Apply this monotonicity to x and y to obtain |a+b|/(1+|a+b|) ≤ (|a|+|b|)/(1+|a|+|b|)."
